  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16:\n\n> bug, in fixtures, we cannot locate stock to existing vise - only model.\n\nWhat happens:\n\n- A setup has a vise.\n- The fixture controls can locate the model on that vise.\n- The fixture controls cannot locate the stock on that vise.\n\nExpected:\n\n- The user can locate the stock on an existing vise, as the user can locate the model.\n- In practice the vise holds the stock, not the finished model. The stock is thus the usual body to locate.\n\nNotes:\n\n- The location change is an undoable command (AGENTS.md \"Everything Is a Command\"). A new command needs its MCP tool or a follow-up issue.\n- The position of the stock against the vise is input to the fixture collision checks and to the carried-workholding check. The work is thus under the safety floor.\n- Issue #2172 changes how the model, the stock and a fixture stand on the floor of the work envelope. This issue touches the same code. Work it after #2172, or stack it on the PR of #2172.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins that the stock can be located on an existing vise, and that undo restores the earlier position.\n- A test pins that the collision checks read the located position of the stock.\n- The same operation is available through MCP, or a follow-up issue names it.\n",
